spec={
'central_state_university_v_aaup_summary':([V],"The Court's per curiam opinion, joined by Stone-Zsela, O'Connor, Scalia, Kennedy, Souter, Thomas, Ginsburg and Breyer (eight Justices). Stevens opposes summary disposition and takes no final federal-merits position.","The holding creates no general immunity for anti-union action and does not adjudicate existing agreements, other bargaining rights, retaliation for protected association or independent state-law protections.","Reverse and remand on the federal equal-protection question; surviving independent state-law questions remain for the Ohio courts."),
'kumho_tire':([F]*4,["Breyer's opinion of the Court, Part I, unanimous.","Breyer's opinion of the Court, Part II, unanimous.","Breyer's Part III-A, joined by Stone-Zsela, O'Connor, Scalia, Kennedy, Souter, Thomas and Ginsburg (eight Justices). Stevens reserves application; this coalition does not establish Part III-B's mandate.","Breyer's Part III-B, joined by O'Connor, Scalia, Kennedy, Souter, Thomas and Ginsburg (seven Justices). Stone-Zsela and Stevens do not join the conforming mandate."],"Original Rule 702 governs; no later amendment, universal technical checklist, finding that misuse caused the accident or categorical rejection of visual inspection is adopted.","The eight-Justice reversal and seven-Justice operative mandate require a disposition sustaining exclusion and the resulting defense summary judgment on this reconsidered proffer, not a new hearing, appointed expert or another appellate determination whether to sustain exclusion."),
'south_central_bell':([F,F,T,T,T],"Chief Justice Stone-Zsela's unanimous opinion of the Court, Parts I–V.","The Court determines no exact refund, replacement assessment, severability result or taxpayer's satisfaction of payment and preservation conditions. It does not reopen binding judgments or decide a new federal damages action.","Reverse and remand for constitutionally adequate relief through lawful state mechanisms; the conditional backward-looking duty and independent prohibition on withdrawing a held-out postpayment remedy remain distinct."),
'jones_v_united_states_merits_1999-03-24':([P,P],"Scalia's opinion of the Court, joined by Stone-Zsela, Stevens, Souter, Thomas and Ginsburg (six Justices). Separate constitutional theories do not supply an additional Court holding.","The sufficient ground is construction of the original carjacking statute and ordinary protections of its aggravated elements. No general constitutional maximum-fact rule, prior-conviction exception, unchanged-maximum minimum rule, universal Guidelines classification or capital-sentencing rule is decided; McMillan and Walton are not overruled.","Vacate the aggravated sentence and remand. Sentencing on the existing indictment and verdict may not exceed the fifteen-year basic maximum. No particular sentence, aggregate calculation, acquittal or authorization of a new aggravated prosecution is ordered."),
'minnesota_v_mille_lacs':([I]*4,"Stevens's opinion of the Court, Parts I–IV, joined by Stone-Zsela, O'Connor, Souter, Ginsburg and Breyer (six Justices).", "Independent presidential revocation under the pleasure clause, particular conservation measures, numerical harvest allocations, private-land access, unrelated criminal conduct and rights beyond the ceded territory remain undecided.","Affirm recognition of the surviving treaty rights and the reviewed declaratory/injunctive framework, subject to lawful, necessary nondiscriminatory conservation measures."),
'brower_v_washington':([X]*3,"Kennedy's unanimous opinion of the Court.","No general private-reimbursement or campaign-duration safe harbor, right to resource parity or transfer of electoral voting power follows. A supported inability to organize or communicate or deliberately disabling calendar requires actual-burden analysis. State-law holdings are not adopted as federal law.","Affirm the presented federal components without a new election, changed tally, injunction, damages or unwinding of reimbursement."),
'united_states_v_rodriguez':([P],"Thomas's opinion of the Court, joined by Stone-Zsela, O'Connor, Kennedy, Souter, Ginsburg and Breyer (seven Justices).", "No broader effects-only venue rule, different charge, number-of-violations question, independent sentence issue or other conviction is decided. Cabrales's alternate-charge reservations remain.","Reverse and remand, restoring the section 924(c) conviction and sentence subject to genuinely unresolved, properly available claims; the continuing kidnapping supports New Jersey venue."),
'conn_v_gabbert':([V],"Chief Justice Stone-Zsela's occupational-merits holding, joined by all eight Associate Justices.","The rule requires no permanent exclusion or financial loss and creates no general immunity for temporary interference. Eight Justices (all but Stevens) also join the confined explanation that an objection to this search's reasonableness falls under the Fourth Amendment; that explanation is not a second sufficient ground absorbing an independent occupational injury. Search validity, privilege, client rights, qualified immunity, absolute immunity and mandatory merits-first sequencing are not decided.","Reverse and remand on the occupational-liberty claim. The separately pleaded Fourth Amendment claim retains its actual procedural position; no new hearing, discovery, damages or revival of an ungranted claim is ordered."),
'mitchell_v_united_states':([P]*3,["Breyer's opinion of the Court, Part I, unanimous.","Breyer's Part II, joined by Stone-Zsela, Stevens, Kennedy, Souter and Ginsburg (six Justices).","Breyer's Part III, joined by Stone-Zsela, Stevens, Kennedy, Souter and Ginsburg (six Justices)."],"The privilege exists while testimony presents a genuine risk of additional criminal punishment; no permanent privilege or ban on lawful voluntary-statement use follows. No quantity-element classification, universal jury rule, mandatory-minimum rule or entitlement to acceptance credit is adopted.","Vacate the sentence and remand for quantity determination from lawful affirmative evidence without the adverse silence inference. No fixed term, automatic minimum, plea withdrawal, acquittal or jury hearing is ordered; consequential components follow their own governing law."),
'murphy_brothers':([F],"Ginsburg's opinion of the Court, joined by Stone-Zsela, Stevens, O'Connor, Kennedy, Souter and Breyer (seven Justices).", "Both original thirty-day branches and the shorter-period direction remain. No valid period is extended, service evasion excused, precise unpresented waiver timing decided, pre-service removal forbidden or later-removability paragraph applied. Timeliness supplies no subject-matter jurisdiction.","Reverse and remand; treat removal as timely and address subject-matter jurisdiction and any other preserved remand ground. Contract merits and fees remain undecided."),
'wyoming_v_houghton':([P],"O'Connor's opinion of the Court, joined by Scalia, Kennedy, Thomas and Breyer (five Justices).", "The holding concerns a detached purse inside the automobile capable of containing the drugs supported by probable cause. It does not authorize a bodily search or decide an effect worn or carried on the person; ownership and personal privacy remain distinct from an applicable exception.","Reverse and remand; passenger ownership cannot sustain the reviewed suppression judgment, but no unconditional conviction reinstatement or disposition of independent available grounds follows."),
'barnes_v_american_tobacco':([F],"Breyer's unanimous opinion of the Court.","No categorical bar on medical monitoring, tobacco class actions, class size or individual differences is adopted. Rule23(a) remains applicable; no independent Amchem adequacy-conflict holding, individual standing adjudication, new limitations or medical-necessity rule, assumed merits jurisdiction or available replacement class is established.","Affirm the reviewed certification denial. The five limitations judgments and sixth plaintiff's monitoring-need judgment remain undisturbed without separately affirming their substantive merits. No named claim, renewed certification or mandatory subclasses are ordered."),
'in_re_sealed_case':([F],"Stevens's unanimous opinion of the Court.","Recognition and overcoming a privilege are distinct. No classified-information, state-secrets, executive-privilege, constitutional-security or other properly asserted privilege claim is decided; no particular agent knowledge, criminal conduct, access impairment, waiver or future arrangement is found.","Affirm the compulsion order subject to ordinary objections, other lawful privileges and concrete security accommodations. No privilege-specific investigative-need showing is imposed."),
'unum_life':([L]*2,"Ginsburg's unanimous opinion of the Court.","The insurance considerations are guideposts, not three indispensable conjunctive elements; independent risk transfer is not decided. Self-funded plans, deemer-clause protection and other timing rules remain open. The agency holding supplies no general federal agency code or automatic ineffectiveness of employer notice; Ward did not press insurance saving for that distinct agency theory.","Affirm the notice-prejudice ruling and reversal of insurer summary judgment; UNUM must prove actual prejudice. Reverse the no-relation agency premise and reconsider any material properly presented actual-agency theory under the corrected rule and policy's written-authorization provision. No benefits or actual-agency finding follows."),
'united_states_v_haggar':([D]*2,["Chief Justice Stone-Zsela's opinion, Parts I–III, unanimous.","Chief Justice Stone-Zsela's Part IV, joined by O'Connor, Scalia, Kennedy, Souter, Thomas and Breyer (seven Justices)."],"The tariff requires United States fabricated components exported ready for assembly without further fabrication, retention of physical identity and no foreign advancement or improvement except assembly and incidental operations including cleaning, lubricating and painting. The allowance reduces duties by qualifying component cost or value, with proportional treatment of specific/compound rates; it does not exempt the entire article. Regulation §10.16(b) permits incidental operations before, during or after assembly, including ordinary final pressing/folding; §10.16(c)'s significant nonassembly processes and unrelated processes retain their introductory conditions despite chemical-treatment examples. Timing after sewing alone does not decide the issue. Informal letters and later administrative doctrines are not decided.","Vacate and remand for the regulation's statutory fit and actual application without categorical nondeference. No regulatory validity, exemption, refund, duty amount, new hearing or finding of missing papers is established."),
'brooks_v_barnes':([X]*3,["Souter's Parts I–II, joined by Stevens, O'Connor, Kennedy, Ginsburg and Breyer (six Justices).","Souter's Part III, unanimous.","Souter's Part III, unanimous; the same-enactment determination is independently sufficient."],"Section2 results and constitutional purpose remain distinct. No violation, plurality system, alternate threshold, racial vote guarantee or new statistical study is ordered; a remedy requires a proved violation and lawful comparison.","Vacate and remand the statutory claim under corrected nomination-opportunity standards; affirm the constitutional judgment on supported purpose findings and the independent same-enactment ground."),
'united_states_v_sun_diamond':([P]*2,"Scalia's unanimous opinion of the Court.","The act must be an official act within §201(a)(3), and circumstantial proof of an act-linked gift may suffice. There is no comprehensive definition of every official act, friendship exemption or permission for gifts barred by other law. No blanket structural-error rule, exhaustive evidentiary-sufficiency ruling or indictment-sufficiency decision is made.","Affirm CountOne's reversal and lawful new-trial remand under an act-linked instruction; no acquittal or final sufficiency determination follows."),
'russell_v_burris':([X]*4,["O'Connor's opinion of the Court, Part I, unanimous."]+["O'Connor's opinion of the Court, Parts II–IV, joined by Stevens, Souter, Ginsburg and Breyer (five Justices)."]*3,"The residual $100 class includes covered judicial offices other than the two named appellate offices. No permanent dollar floor, aggregate pool across committees, universal candidate-conduit finding or approval of materially different financing burdens follows.","Affirm invalidation of the seven named statewide $300 limits and two named appellate-office $100 applications; reverse the residual categorical invalidation and the ordinary-PAC and exact small-donor differential rulings on their stated grounds. No replacement ceiling, refunds, damages or retrospective enforcement direction is ordered; consistent severability treatment remains."),
'bank_of_america':([K],"Kennedy's opinion of the Court, joined by Stone-Zsela, O'Connor, Scalia, Souter, Thomas, Ginsburg and Breyer (eight Justices).", "No asset/contribution valuation error or higher outside bid is found. Lawful unappealed §1121 proposal exclusivity does not resolve §1129 substantive confirmability. General new-value survival and complete conditions remain open; no auction, bidder, automatic exclusivity termination or universal valuation method is required. Stone-Zsela's further market-exposure proposal is not Court law.","Reverse the confirmation judgment and remand for lawful plan proceedings removing this exclusive-opportunity defect; the unappealed exclusivity ruling, classification and accepted valuations are not reopened."),
'el_paso_natural_gas':([I,F],"Thomas's unanimous opinion of the Court.","The rule addresses the invoked Price-Anderson federal channel, not every mining case or ordinary tribal-exhaustion question. Uncovered claims retain actual jurisdiction, substantive tribal-authority, proper-party, immunity and equitable conditions; no unexamined treaty right or ultimate claim is decided.","Vacate and remand for federal determination of Price-Anderson coverage; set aside the unappealed enlargement and restore partial injunctions to their preappeal position without a new merits adjudication of their propriety."),
'ins_v_aguirre':([G]*4,["Breyer's opinion of the Court, Parts I–II, unanimous."]*3+["Breyer's Part III, joined by all eight Associate Justices. Stone-Zsela joins the disposition only and adds no rationale vote."],"Political purpose, context and conduct remain material under the Board's actual standard. Neither agency status nor foreign-affairs expertise supplies automatic correctness. The separate discretionary asylum denial does not become a statutory automatic bar; no translation defect or entitlement to a new hearing is presumed.","Reverse the mandatory additional judicial conditions and remand without a final withholding/asylum decision, stay, removal instruction or ordered new hearing. The existing BIA motion follows its own lawful channel."),
'redmon_v_united_states':([P],"O'Connor's opinion of the Court, joined by Stone-Zsela, Stevens, Souter and Ginsburg (five Justices). Only Stevens, Souter and Ginsburg additionally conclude that this inspection was a search; that conclusion is not Court law.", "No general right in curbside garbage, rule for a collector's private inspection, private-search reporting rule or protection for publicly accessible containers outside protected residential space is decided. Limited private approach access is not itself general police permission.","Vacate and remand for the actual protected-space, exposure and intrusion inquiry without deciding the ultimate search application. No automatic exclusion, acquittal, release, plea withdrawal, sentence or evidentiary hearing is ordered."),
'pension_benefit_guaranty':([K]*3,["Souter's Part I, joined by all eight Associate Justices; Stone-Zsela does not join the tax-priority remand.","Souter's Part II, unanimous.","Souter's Part III, joined by all eight Associate Justices; Stone-Zsela does not join the valuation remand."],"Section412(n) concerns covered unpaid required contributions exceeding $1million and a lien arising on the sixtieth day after the installment due date. The tax instruction concerns an amount with respect to which that lien is imposed and imports rules similar to §4068(c),(d),(e). The lower finding that the installment was due fewer than sixty days prepetition, and the preserved no-lien/stay alternative, remain unresolved by this Court. No universal estate-benefit prerequisite, exclusion of postpetition statutory wrongs, PBGC methodology, duplicate discounting or universal pension rate is approved.","Vacate tax priority and the $124,441,000 valuation for lawful construction and liability/allowance review; affirm denial of additional administrative priority for prepetition-service debt. Preserve the allowed postpetition-service component and AppealFund limit. No priority, amount, lien attachment, new rule or hearing is ordered."),
'saenz_v_roe':([V]*2,"Kennedy's opinion of the Court, joined by Stone-Zsela, Stevens, O'Connor, Scalia, Souter, Ginsburg and Breyer (eight Justices).", "Bona fide residence verification and equal eligibility conditions remain enforceable. The Court establishes no national benefit amount or general welfare entitlement and does not reopen Slaughter-House's broader construction.","Affirm the preliminary injunction against California's first-year prior-State ceiling; no permanent decree, damages or fixed benefit amount is entered."),
'clinton_v_goldsmith':([F],"Kennedy's unanimous opinion of the Court.","No merits ruling on constitutional personnel-action objections or adequacy of a different administrative/judicial route is made. The AllWrits Act protects actual or potential jurisdiction without supplying general military-administration supervision.","Reverse and dissolve the injunction; the court-martial findings and sentence remain undisturbed. Independent channels retain their own jurisdictional and remedial conditions."),
'florida_v_white':([P],"Thomas's opinion of the Court, joined by O'Connor, Scalia, Kennedy, Souter and Breyer (six Justices).", "The readily movable automobile and public-place seizure limit the rule. No general contraband-property exception, protected-premises entry authority, subsequent search, retention, hearing or final-forfeiture result is decided.","Reverse and remand from the federal warrant/additional-emergency suppression ground. No unconditional conviction reinstatement, admission of every item or forfeiture award follows; independent available grounds remain."),
'hunt_v_cromartie':([X,F],["Ginsburg's Parts II–III, joined by Stone-Zsela, Stevens, Souter and Breyer (five Justices).","Ginsburg's Part I, unanimous at this procedural level, without agreement that the predominance claim may proceed."],"Predominance alone supplies neither constitutional injury nor a reason for trial. The Court does not finally validate the map, create a new claim, deem an unknown claim forfeited or independently decide the State's own summary-judgment motion.","Vacate the summary judgment and injunction unanimously; the five-Justice mandate permits only actually presented independently cognizable claims under their own elements and ordinary procedure."),
'new_jersey_v_new_york':([E],"The Court's unsigned implementing decree, No.120,Original, May17,1999, 526 U.S.589; no numerical vote or individual lineup is announced.","The six-part instrument, full182-course perimeter and appended December1,1998 map are incorporated as the complete geographic decree; approximate acreage or an additional separately counted pier parcel cannot replace it. No prescription reopening or new municipal-regulation, taxation, private-title, federal-monument, public-access, damages or later-reclamation holding is made.","ParagraphI enjoins NewYork's enforcement of its laws or assertion of sovereignty over the territory assigned to NewJersey within paragraphIV. ParagraphV retains implementation jurisdiction; paragraphVI divides equally the SpecialMaster's and assistants' compensation and the Master's litigation expenses."),
'ruhrgas_ag':([F],"Scalia's unanimous opinion of the Court.","The bounded route applies to removed and originally filed actions, respects statutory remand commands and review bars, and creates no universal sequence or preclusion rule. No contested merits may be decided on assumed jurisdiction.","Reverse and remand for review of the personal-jurisdiction dismissal under the correct sequencing rule. The Court permits the choice of inquiry but does not affirm actual contacts or ultimate personal-jurisdiction conclusions, decide removal grounds or order state-court remand."),
'maine_green_party':([F,X],["Stone-Zsela's concurrence and Stevens's dissent joined by Kennedy, Souter and Ginsburg directly agree on this bounded proposition (five Justices), across the judgment division.",None],"The majority preservation proposition concerns refinement of an existing legal argument, not an established exclusively local philosophy or permission to invent new summary-judgment facts. No general retention threshold or constitutional ballot-access application receives five votes.","Affirm,5–4, by Stone-Zsela,O'Connor,Scalia,Thomas and Breyer. Four rely on preservation and Stone-Zsela on contextual merits; no logical subset supplies a Marks rationale. The judgment orders no reopening, recognition, injunction or new election."),
'california_dental':([A]*4,["Souter's statutory-coverage opinion, unanimous."]+["Souter's competitive-analysis opinion, joined by Stone-Zsela, O'Connor, Scalia and Thomas (five Justices)."]*3,"No final liability, professional immunity, universal market-definition trial, fixed sequence of labels or measured service-output proof is required. Supported agency findings retain statutory review protection. No majority decides whether the NinthCircuit may complete review on the existing record or must direct Commission reconsideration.","Sustain FTC coverage unanimously; vacate both price- and quality-advertising liability determinations,5–4, and remand through the NinthCircuit for fuller restraint-specific consideration. The four-Justice appellate-choice discussion and Stone-Zsela's Commission-only direction are separate noncontrolling remedies."),
'cleveland_v_policy':([L]*2,"Stevens's unanimous opinion of the Court.","Ordinary qualification, accommodation, discrimination and defense requirements remain. No general judicial-estoppel doctrine for purely factual contradictions or every statutory relationship is adopted; good faith alone does not answer a material factual inconsistency.","Vacate and remand, allowing an adequate explanation that the employer may contest. No compulsory trial, liability, award, benefits revision or automatic Texas-claim revival follows."),
'davis_v_monroe':([V]*3,["Ginsburg's PartI, joined by Stone-Zsela, Stevens, O'Connor, Souter and Breyer (six Justices).","Ginsburg's PartII, joined by Stevens, O'Connor, Souter and Breyer (five Justices). Stone-Zsela does not join the severe-or-pervasive threshold.","Ginsburg's PartIII, joined by Stone-Zsela, Stevens, O'Connor, Souter and Breyer (six Justices)."],"Notice, culpability, control, sex-based discrimination, educational deprivation and causal compensable injury are independent. Ordinary negligence, policy breach, peer attendance or unsuccessful reasonable correction alone do not establish liability. No general agency/defense code or Stone-Zsela reporting-failure proposal becomes controlling; teacher-attribution routes remain distinct.","Reverse the categorical dismissal and remand for ordinary proceedings under the sufficient recipient-own-wrong route. No compulsory trial, damages, particular discipline, individual-capacity recovery or reopening of unrelated claims is ordered."),
'hanlon_v_berger':([P,P,V,V],["O'Connor's PartI, unanimous.","O'Connor's PartII, unanimous.","O'Connor's PartIII, joined by Scalia, Kennedy, Souter, Thomas, Ginsburg and Breyer (seven Justices).","O'Connor's PartIV, joined by all eight Associate Justices; Stevens does not join PartIII's separate immunity direction, and Stone-Zsela does not join PartIV."],"No ranch-wide privacy, categorical broadcast rule, image-seizure rule or conclusion about every recording is adopted. Improper commercial purpose alone does not eliminate open fields. The immunity applies to the reviewed media-enterprise theory, not every distinct preserved residential entry/search; no waived claim is revived.","Vacate the reviewed federal-official component,8–1, and remand with the seven-Justice personal-immunity direction. Private-media joint action/damages, WiretapAct, state claims and publication-injunction rulings remain outside the disposition."),
'wilson_v_layne':([P,V],["Scalia's PartI, unanimous.","Scalia's PartII, joined by O'Connor,Kennedy,Souter,Thomas,Ginsburg and Breyer (seven Justices)."],"Genuine reasonable assistance, consent and independently lawful access remain distinct from unrelated media entry. No identical-case requirement, future media-access privilege or general image-seizure conclusion is adopted. Conduct-date notice remains separate from present constitutional law.","Affirm personal immunity on the reviewed April16,1992 media-entry damages theory,7–2. Individual responsibility and injury would remain necessary in an available claim; separate probable-cause and force rulings are not reopened.")}
# Normalize readable spacing in manually supplied compact legal references.
def clean(s):
 if not s:return s
 for a,b in {'Rule23':'Rule 23','Section2':'Section 2','CountOne':'Count One','Section412':'Section 412','$1million':'$1 million','AppealFund':'Appeal Fund','AllWrits':'All Writs','No.120,Original':'No. 120, Original','May17,1999':'May 17, 1999','full182-course':'full 182-course','December1,1998':'December 1, 1998','ParagraphI':'Paragraph I','paragraphIV':'paragraph IV','ParagraphV':'Paragraph V','paragraphVI':'paragraph VI','NewYork':'New York','NewJersey':'New Jersey','SpecialMaster':'Special Master','NinthCircuit':'Ninth Circuit','PartI':'Part I','PartII':'Part II','PartIII':'Part III','PartIV':'Part IV','WiretapAct':'Wiretap Act','April16,1992':'April 16, 1992'}.items():s=s.replace(a,b)
 s=re.sub(r',(?=[A-Za-z0-9])',', ',s)
 s=re.sub(r'(?<=\d), (?=\d{3}(?:\D|$))', ',', s)
 s=s.replace('U.S.589','U.S. 589').replace('§4068(c),(d),(e)','§4068(c), (d), and (e)')
 return s
files=[]
for n in [6,7,8]:
 files += [(n,x) for x in re.findall(r'^FILE (.+)$',(W/f'compact_{n}.txt').read_text(),re.M)]
entries=[];coverage=[]
for chunk,fn in files:
 raw=(R/'records'/fn).read_text();p=raw.split('## Public Projection',1)[1]
 source=hashlib.sha256((R/'records'/fn).read_bytes()).hexdigest();head=raw.splitlines()[0].split('**Case and dockets:** ',1)[1]
 date=re.search(r'1999-\d\d-\d\d',raw.splitlines()[1]).group()
 if '_certiorari_' in fn:
  coverage.append({'file':fn,'chunk':chunk,'date':date,'status':'exclude','reason':'Separate unsigned access grant; expressly no substantive holding and no opinion.','source_sha256':source})
  entries.append({'file':fn,'area':None,'status':'exclude','reason':'Separate certiorari grant establishes no substantive holding.','text':''});continue
 key=next(k for k in spec if fn.startswith(k));areas,auths,limits,remedy=spec[key];limits=clean(limits);remedy=clean(remedy)
 h=p.split('## Holdings',1)[1].split('## Precedent Treatment',1)[0].strip();qs=re.split(r'^#{3,4} ',h,flags=re.M)[1:]
 if len(qs)!=len(areas):raise ValueError((fn,len(qs),areas))
 case=head.split(';')[0].split(', No.')[0];dockets=head[len(case):].lstrip(',; ');dockets=re.sub(r'; OT1998\.?$', '.',dockets)
 if fn.startswith('new_jersey_v_new_york'):case+=', 526 U.S. 589'
 ident=f'#### {case}\n\n**Docket or dockets:** {dockets}\n**Decided:** {date}.\n\n'
 groups={}
 for j,q in enumerate(qs):
  title,body=q.split('\n',1);title=re.sub(r'^[IVX]+(?:-[AB])?\.\s*','',title)
  pars=[z.strip() for z in body.split('\n\n') if z.strip()];authority=clean(auths[j] if isinstance(auths,list) else auths)
  rule=next((z for z in pars if re.match(r'\*\*(?:Holding and operative rule[:.]|Operative rule[:.])',z)),None)
  if key=='maine_green_party' and j==1:
   judgment=next(z for z in pars if z.startswith('**Judgment without controlling rationale:**')).split('**Judgment without controlling rationale:**',1)[1].strip()
   text=f'##### {title}\n\n**Authority of the judgment:** '+judgment+' The affirming Justices are Stone-Zsela, O\'Connor, Scalia, Thomas and Breyer.\n'
  else:
   if not rule:raise ValueError((fn,j,'missing rule'))
   rule=re.sub(r'^\*\*[^*]+\*\*\s*','',rule)
   field='Independent alternative holding' if key=='brooks_v_barnes' and j==2 else 'Holding'
   afield='Proposition-level authority for alternative holding' if field.startswith('Independent') else 'Proposition-level authority'
   text=f'##### {title}\n\n**{field}:** {rule}\n\n**{afield}:** {authority}\n'
  for z in pars:
   if z.startswith('**Independently sufficient alternative holding:**'):
    text+='\n**Independent alternative holding:** '+z.split('**Independently sufficient alternative holding:**',1)[1].strip()+'\n\n**Proposition-level authority for alternative holding:** Chief Justice Stone-Zsela\'s unanimous opinion of the Court, Part IV.\n'
   elif z.startswith('**Limits and questions not reached:**'):text+='\n'+z+'\n'
   elif z.startswith('**Precedent treatment:**'):text+='\n**Treatment of earlier authority:** '+z.split('**Precedent treatment:**',1)[1].strip()+'\n'
  groups.setdefault(areas[j],[]).append(text)
 treatment=p.split('## Precedent Treatment',1)[1].split('## Law After Decision',1)[0].strip()
 primary=next((a for a in groups if a!=F),next(iter(groups)))
 for area,blocks in groups.items():
  text=ident+'\n'.join(blocks)
  if area==primary:text+='\n**Limits and questions not reached:** '+limits+'\n\n**Operative remedy or transition:** '+remedy+'\n\n**Treatment of earlier authority:**\n\n'+treatment+'\n'
  if len(groups)>1:
   text+='\nFor the other questions and complete operative scope in '+case+', '+date+', '+dockets.rstrip('.')+', see '+', '.join(a for a in groups if a!=area)+'.\n'
  if key=='california_dental':
   text+='\n##### Authority of the institutional remand allocation\n\n**Authority of the judgment:** Five Justices vacate both advertising-liability components and require fuller consideration. Souter, O\'Connor, Scalia and Thomas would leave the Ninth Circuit to choose existing-record assessment or Commission reconsideration; Stone-Zsela requires Commission inquiry. Neither institutional direction has five votes, and the common judgment adopts neither allocation as controlling.\n'
  entries.append({'file':fn,'area':area,'text':text,'status':'include'})
 coverage.append({'file':fn,'chunk':chunk,'date':date,'status':'include','areas':list(groups),'questions':len(qs),'source_sha256':source})
(W/'chunk678_entries.json').write_text(json.dumps(entries,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2)+'\n');(W/'chunk678_coverage.json').write_text(json.dumps(coverage,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2)+'\n')
print('records',len(coverage),'included',sum(x['status']=='include' for x in coverage),'area entries',sum(x['status']=='include' for x in entries),'source questions',sum(x.get('questions',0) for x in coverage))
